course: dictionary
lesson: 9082
title: Slow: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word slow can mean different things, so read the words around it to find the right meaning. «Much of Earth's fresh water is frozen in ice sheets, and glaciers, slow rivers of ice.» Rivers of ice cannot run fast, so slow here means moving very gradually, taking a long time to move.
explain: Slow can also be a verb. «Big ones work behind fences or slow down and stop near people.» To slow down means to go less fast, which is why robots near people must do it. Try your meaning in the sentence: does «slow down and stop» still make sense with «go less fast»? It does.
explain: Sometimes slow describes how something happens, not how fast something moves. «Slow blinks mean a cat feels safe with you.» A slow blink is a relaxed, gentle blink, so the meaning here is calm and unhurried. Ask yourself what the clue words tell you about the feeling.
fact: Slow means not fast; it takes a long time to move or to do something.
fact: To slow down means to go less fast.
fact: A slow clock or watch shows a time earlier than the real time.
fact: Slow can be used about a person who is not quick to learn or understand, but this can be unkind to say.
fact: Slow changes form: slower, slowest, and slowly, as in «in slow motion» and «slow and steady».
exercise: «Much of Earth's fresh water is frozen in ice sheets, and glaciers, slow rivers of ice.» In this sentence, what does slow mean? | Cold and hard to touch | Very fast and dangerous | Wet and muddy | *Moving very gradually, taking a long time to move
exercise: Which words mean to go less fast? | Jump | *Slow down | Stop | Speed up
exercise: A slow clock is wrong. What does a slow clock show? | It stops completely | The exact right time | *A time earlier than the real time | A time later than the real time, and then it runs ahead
test: What is the comparative form of slow, the word for more slow? | Slowly | Slowest | Slowing | *Slower
test: «Its whole body has slowed down to save energy.» What does slowed down mean here? | Broke into pieces | Fell into a deep sleep forever | Got faster and busier | *Went less fast, so it moved and worked more gently
exam: Which phrase from the lessons means at a pace that is not fast? | Fast and furious | Wide and round | *Slow and steady | Quick and clever
